// `slice` is overloaded: a string slice is a string, a list slice is a list.
// With an untyped parameter, the static pass types the result as the join of
// both (`string | list`), so a string consumer accepts it and the choice is
// made at run time.
firstTwo(s) = characters(slice(s, 1, 2))
middle(s) = slice(s, 2, 3)
(firstTwo("abc"), middle("abcd"), listFrom(middle([7, 8, 9, 10])))
// ➔ (["a", "b"], "bc", [8, 9])
